            <title>The U.S. Has Lost Measles Elimination Status. Here’s What That Means for Chaffee County</title>
            <description>On Nov. 17, the Pan American Health Organization announced that the United States has lost the measles elimination status it earned in 2000. After 26 years, measles is once again able to spread continuously within the United States.</description>
